\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The cut twist on five torus signs}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For the sign torus and spanning-tree gauge of
\ref{fdip-00UA}, take direction one and #{z=-1}.
The cut is #{x_1=1}. Its crossing links are
#{U_1(1,0)=a} and #{U_1(1,1)=d}, so the twist is
##{(a,b,c,d,e)\longmapsto(-a,b,c,-d,e).}
The three fixed tree links remain one. The horizontal
Polyakov trace based at #{(0,0)} is #{a}, and changes
sign. The positive edges remain separately labeled
even when a lattice period is two.}
